teal green as primary with a warm terracotta accent and a cream background — and writing one reusable CSS block using custom properties for consistency across all pages. I'm also planning the shared header with an announcement bar, logo with \"Since 1999\" tagline, and nav links for Yoga Mats, Props & Blocks, Bolsters, Studio Bulk, and Sale.\n\nNow I'm inventing a plausible product lineup with prices, ratings, review counts, and badges like \"Studio favorite\" and \"Bulk 10+ save 20%\" to make the featured section feel authentic, plus urgency copy and social proof stats for credibility.\n\nI want to keep the JavaScript lightweight — cart count, a free shipping progress bar, FAQ accordion, quantity steppers, tabs, and a simple email discount modal triggered by time delay or exit intent using localStorage, avoiding anything heavy.\n\nWriting shared CSS...\n\nAdding nav and header styles...\n\nI'm avoiding external image URLs since they might break, so I'll build gradient-based placeholder tiles with simple inline SVG shapes for product cards instead—safer and self-contained.\n\nWriting SVG shapes...\n\nNow I need to write out full pages, each self-contained with header and footer, carefully escaping quotes since everything needs to fit into a single-line JSON string.\n\nWriting shared CSS styles...\n\nAdding header nav and search styles...\n\nAdding hero section styles...\n\nAdding trust bar styles...\n\nAdding card thumbnail and badge styles...\n\nAdding form and FAQ styles...\n\nAdding footer styles and modal overlay...\n\nAdding responsive breakpoints and mobile nav behavior, then starting the shared header markup with the promo bar and logo.\n\nI'm building the main nav links plus a search input and cart icon, and deciding to keep only a handful of real pages while pointing other nav items toward the single yoga-mats collection to avoid dead ends.\n\nI'll settle on directory-style paths for each page—home, collections/all, the product page, wholesale, about, contact, and cart—so links resolve cleanly. Now I'm building the shared footer with the logo and navigation links.\n\nNow I'm finishing the footer with copyright and trust badges, then writing the shared JS for cart count persistence, add-to-cart handling, and popups.\n\nFor the homepage hero, I'm drafting copy with a trust-building eyebrow line, a strong H1 about studio-grade mats direct from source, supporting ticks on pricing/shipping/returns, and dual CTAs pointing to the best-sellers collection and wholesale page, plus a review rating. Alongside it, I'm sketching a highlighted \"Studio Starter Kit\" offer card with a savings badge and bundled pricing.\n\nNow I'm mapping out the rest of the page structure: a trust bar with company stats, a bestsellers grid with badges and bulk notes, category tiles, a wholesale section with a quote form and testimonials, and a \"Why YogaDirect\" section covering manufacturing heritage and community.\n\nThen I'm listing sections for reviews, FAQ, an email capture band with a discount offer, and a sticky mobile CTA button. I'm drafting the actual product data now — pricing, ratings, bulk discounts, and color swatches for items like the Pro Grip mat, cork mat, foam blocks, and cotton strap.\n\nI'm rounding out the product roster with a bolster, blanket, cork wheel, and a bundled starter kit with savings noted, then planning a 12-product collection page with filtering.\n\nI'm sketching out the rest of the site: the collection page's sidebar and sort controls, a product detail page with variant swatches and bulk pricing tiers, a wholesale page with a quote form and tier table, plus About, Contact, and Cart pages covering the standard content each needs.\n\nFor the cart page, I'm adding a shipping progress bar, order bump upsells, a discount code field, checkout button, trust badges, and a \"you may also like\" section. I'm also noting I'll paraphrase the client's own About page copy rather than copy verbatim, since it's their content to reuse for their own site improvement.\n\nWriting thumbnail styling with gradients...\n\nSketching more icon SVGs...\n\nNow I'm planning to write out each page's HTML content, along with a short improvements list, and considering adding a brief JSON-LD schema for SEO on the product page while keeping it minimal.\n\nWriting form submission JS...\n\nI'll switch to hiding the form and revealing a success message by toggling display, avoiding extra quote conflicts, then include a sticky mobile bar with free shipping and a shop button. Now I'm drafting the full homepage body starting with the header and hero section.\n\nAdding the review stats and building out the product card with pricing badge and starter kit details...\n\nFilling in the bundle contents, pricing with strikethrough, bulk discount note, and add-to-cart button, then moving on to the trust band, bestsellers grid, and category tiles sections.\n\nI'm planning the wholesale signup form fields and trust bullets, then the \"why us\" and reviews grids, FAQ, email band, footer, and modal, being careful to use text like \"1/4 in\" instead of a raw quote character to keep the JSON clean. Now I'm writing out the final JSON structure with the popup modal markup.\n\nAdding the discount popup content...\n\nthen I'll finalize the cart page with static quantity, subtotal, and progress bar logic, plus a sticky buy bar for the product page that shows the price on mobile.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I should go ahead and fetch the website to see what's there.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":""},{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The fetch only returned minimal plain text, so I'll try again with a different approach to see if I can get more structured content, maybe checking other pages.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":1,"signature":""},{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Since I only have the homepage content, I'm planning to build out a full multi-page site for YogaDirect—a