Cart buttons\",\"Why\":\"Social proof (ratings/review counts) and price anchoring (was/now pricing) increase add-to-cart rates, and surfacing products on the homepage shortens the path to purchase\"},{\"What\":\"Added a Shop by Category grid with visual tiles for mats, bolsters, blocks, straps, blankets, and meditation gear\",\"Why\":\"Visual category navigation helps visitors self-segment quickly, improving product findability and reducing exits from the homepage\"},{\"What\":\"Created a dedicated Wholesale/Studio page with a quote request form, volume-discount messaging, and B2B testimonials, plus promotional banners for it on the homepage and category page\",\"Why\":\"Studios and bulk buyers represent the highest-revenue customer segment for a company that has 'supplied studios since 1999'; a structured lead-capture funnel converts these high-value visitors instead of losing them\"},{\"What\":\"Added an email capture section offering 10% off the first order\",\"Why\":\"Email capture monetizes the ~97% of visitors who don't buy on their first visit, enabling remarketing that typically drives 20-30% of e-commerce revenue\"},{\"What\":\"Added customer testimonials with names, roles, and star ratings, plus an aggregate '4.8/5 from 12,000+ reviews' claim area\",\"Why\":\"Third-party validation from both individual yogis and studio owners addresses both B2C and B2B buyer objections\"},{\"What\":\"Built an improved category page (/yoga-mats) with breadcrumbs, sort controls, product count, bulk-pack SKUs, and a bottom-of-page wholesale CTA\",\"Why\":\"A well-structured category page with sorting and social proof is where most purchase decisions happen; adding a 10-pack SKU and wholesale CTA upsells volume buyers\"},{\"What\":\"Rewrote the About page around the brand story with a stats bar (25+ years, 500K+ customers) and a closing shop CTA\",\"Why\":\"About pages are among the most-visited pages for trust-checking shoppers; ending with a CTA converts that trust into sales rather than dead-ending the visit\"},{\"What\":\"Added SEO-optimized titles and meta descriptions with keywords, prices, and offers on every page\",\"Why\":\"Better titles/descriptions improve organic click-through rates from search, increasing qualified traffic at zero acquisition cost\"},{\"What\":\"Made the entire site mobile-responsive with prominent tap-friendly buttons, a persistent cart button, and a site-wide search bar\",\"Why\":\"Mobile typically accounts for 60%+ of e-commerce traffic; friction-free mobile navigation, search, and checkout entry points directly lift mobile conversion\"},{\"What\":\"Displayed the toll-free phone number, support email, and business hours in the footer alongside payment method and security assurances\",\"Why\":\"Visible human contact options and payment trust marks reduce cart abandonment, particularly for larger studio orders where buyers want reassurance\"}]}","refusal":null,"reasoning":"I should start by fetching the website to see what's there.The fetch only gave me limited content and no links to follow, so I can't crawl subpages beyond the homepage the user gave me. I'll work with what I know about YogaDirect—a yoga mats and props retailer since 1999—and build an improved homepage plus a couple key pages like a product listing and about page.\n\nI'm planning the homepage structure: announcement bar with free shipping details, header with search and category nav, a hero section with CTA, trust badges, featured product cards, category grid, a wholesale/B2B section, testimonials, and email signup, all with complete HTML and inline CSS in one JSON response.\n\nI'll also build a category page and an about-us page alongside the homepage, keeping products realistic (mats, bolsters, blocks, straps) and reusing shared CSS across all three for consistency, writing the HTML without newlines to keep the JSON single-line.Since I only have the homepage content to work from, I'll build an improved multi-page site drawing on general 